        "original_id": "ebd99899-38ec-526f-b2c2-0ecf5e4fae89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Vanderbilt University, Emory University, Methodist Episcopal Church\n- People: Cornelius Vanderbilt, John Emory, William Ridley Wills\n- Places: Oxford, Georgia, metropolitan Atlanta, Brownsville, Tennessee\n- Topics: university founding, naming, relocation, education, literary groups\n\nFacts:\n- Emory University was founded as Emory College in 1836 in Oxford, Georgia by the Methodist Episcopal Church and was named in honor of Methodist bishop John Emory.\n- Vanderbilt University was founded in 1873 and was named in honor of Cornelius Vanderbilt, who provided its initial $1 million endowment despite never having been to the South.\n- Emory University relocated to metropolitan Atlanta in 1915 and was rechartered from Emory College as Emory University.\n- William Ridley Wills was born in Brownsville, Tennessee on March 4, 1897.\n- William Ridley Wills was a graduate of Vanderbilt University and a member of the Fugitive literary group.",
